{
  "description": "What the listener app's outbox does with an item after each answer (contract §3, R9; corrections 4, 7 and 11). Each row is one case: the item kind and the answer (HTTP, HTTP_WITH_UNREADABLE_BODY for a 200 the app could not read, NO_ANSWER, PHONE_FAULT); for HTTP the status, or for a default row the status class; the error code (null: any code, or none); the Retry-After in seconds (null: no header). For one kind the most specific row decides: the status with the code, else the status with a null code, else the status class. action and wait are what the policy returns for exactly that case. wait: SECONDS (a Retry-After clamped to 1 to 3,600, or the default: 3 for a 409, 60 for a 429), BACKOFF (min(30 x 2^(n-1), 1800) seconds x a random factor from 0.5 to 1 after the n-th failure), RANDOM_SECONDS (a deferred clip whose 502, 503 or 504 carries no Retry-After waits a random 60 to 300 seconds), or null. Groups: clips (DEFERRED_CLIP), follow-ups (STATION_CHOICE, ENGAGEMENT, RECOGNITION_REPORT) and crash reports (CLIENT_ERROR_REPORT, which is never reported about). A crash report answered 426, which POST /client-errors never gives, is kept and backs off",
